---
run: round-trip
fixpoint: executed
why: 30V section 5 - the whole-product proof of the receipt-rooted why. One block publishes a receipt into the session store; the later blocks read it back and render the total surface (`--receipt-last`), its `--json` register, and `--all`, which is the shape no single drive can demonstrate. The transcript IS the assertion (`loom-transcript-is-what-the-user-saw`); --all byte-identity and --json well-formedness are read straight off the goldened both-streams output, and the explicit file root and both address directions are pinned by receipt_state.rs.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# One MEASURED site, which is the whole fixture requirement: a run publishes a receipt only when
# its intake ADMITTED records, and a framed stream with none is NoObservation.
foobar sync-certs /etc/nginx/certs

-- foobar.oracle.sh --
foobar__is_converged() {
   verb="$1"; shift
   case "$verb" in
   sync-certs) foobar status --certs-current -- "$1" ;;
   *) return 2 ;;
   esac
}

-- probe-results.txt --
site 0 effect=holds rc=0

-- replay --
$ export DORC_SEED=0

$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --pre-source foobar.oracle.sh --results - < probe-results.txt
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
